# WHAT IT CHANGES FOR THE PHONE
#   All Metal 4 feedback callbacks run on ONE serial queue (g_feedback_q). The completion of an upload batch used to call res_commit() there: it applies the residency set's removals of
#   the batch's staging and waits for g_res_commit_mu, which the encode thread also holds for every queue commit. A slow residency commit delayed the fence / present completions queued
#   behind it (the same pattern was reported as a freeze of Ocarina of Time after loading a save on an iPhone 18 Pro Max; cause still open upstream). Now the feedback handler hands the
#   staging to a serial worker (res_commit_q) that removes it under ONE acquisition of the commit lock and frees the upload slot afterwards (up_complete). New diagnostics:
#   "[RED] slow residency commit: ..." and "[RED] slow queue commit: ... at <site> on thread ..." for commits of 100 ms or more (first 20 of each kind, then every 100th), measured outside
#   the lock: the line to look for in the next Ocarina log. Default: on, no switch.
#
# HAND-MERGED: one hunk (this tree's snap_take carries a commit-options variable upstream's does not). Left out: docs and game notes.
# RISK: low-medium. NOT run on a device. Shader chain id untouched.
#
# Apply with: patch -p1, to the tree out-stage/out-engine/engine + engine-patches/0401..0415 and the candidates numbered below this one, in the order of the numbers of this folder.

